.TH kodak-i2000-fw 1 "27 Aug 2026" "kodak_i2000" "SANE Scanner Access Now Easy"
.IX kodak-i2000-fw
.SH NAME
kodak-i2000-fw \- verify or extract Kodak i2400 volatile firmware
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kodak-i2000-fw verify
.I source
.PP
.B kodak-i2000-fw extract
.I source output
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kodak-i2000-fw
authenticates the exact Kodak i2400 v4.14 firmware resources used by the
native
.B kodak_i2000
backend. The source may be the vendor's devicemanager container or an existing
compact bundle. Proprietary firmware is not distributed with SANE.
.PP
The
.B extract
command writes a compact, non-executable bundle containing only the seven
images used by volatile i2400 startup: LOADER, FPGA, SCANNER0 through SCANNER3,
and SCANNER. It omits the device-manager ELF code, BOOTER, BOOTIMAGE, and
unrelated resources. The output is created with mode 0600 and extraction
refuses to overwrite an existing file.
.PP
Before accepting either format, the tool checks the i2400 package identity,
expected sizes, and compiled-in SHA-256 values. The compact format additionally
binds the USB identity and scanner version in a versioned header, includes a
whole-payload digest, and is rechecked resource by resource when opened.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Set
.B firmware-source
in
.I kodak_i2000.conf
to the compact output path. The backend reads it only when the attached
040a:601c i2400 reports firmware ID zero, one, or two. A warm scanner at
firmware ID three does not stage the file.
.PP
The supported path is volatile. The tool and backend do not implement
persistent booter programming, flash writes, NVRAM writes, or the external
SCANNERX override.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
kodak-i2000-fw extract /opt/kodak/kds_i2000/lib/devicemanager.so \
  /var/lib/sane/i2400-v4.14.kfw
kodak-i2000-fw verify /var/lib/sane/i2400-v4.14.kfw
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sane (7),
.BR scanimage (1)
